-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 33, RULES 29 TO 46: INSPECTION; EVIDENCE; SALVAGE; SUMMONS; LIMITATION ACTIONS; REFERENCES TO THE REGISTRAR; MARINE INSURANCE.  LAYER 1.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
-- Written with a macro builder that quotes the source lines and writes the @ref; the builder is not part of this row, so edit this file directly.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Every decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the Rule says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the Rule says no in its own words: a "means" definition, a flat negative, an "if" or "where" condition unmet,
--                a period fixed in the text's own words and missed.
--   NOTHING      the Rule does not answer: a duty not yet met, a power limited by its own wording, a list that is not closed, a silence.
-- A period is a Period constant plus a function over the last day of the period.  The last day is an INPUT, `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`:
-- the party states it as counted under Order 3, Rule 3.  Where the period is "the time fixed by the decree" or "such other period as the Court may direct",
-- the last day is the input as the decree or the direction fixes it.
-- SEAMS.  Inputs taken from outside this range: O 3 r 3 (the last day); O 9 r 9 and r 24; O 11 r 2; O 13 r 2 and 3; O 15 r 4, 10 and 11;
-- O 21 r 27 and 28; O 26 r 3.
-- ANCHORS this range offers to other Parts: `o 33 r 36(1) the person seeking relief is the claimant in a limitation action` (Order 44),
-- `o 33 r 42 a reference is heard under this Rule` (Fourth Schedule).

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 33 -- Admiralty proceedings and marine insurance claims: rules 29 to 46`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rules 29 to 35 -- inspection, examination of witnesses, order to attend, salvage, summons, agreements, originating applications`
