      `the preliminary acts have been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 30(4) an order authorising an examination of a witness cannot yet be made for want of the preliminary acts` MEANS
    IF `preliminary acts fall to be filed under Rule 18 in the action`
    THEN IF `the preliminary acts have been filed`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the preliminary acts have been filed": they have been filed
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (4) speaks only of actions in which preliminary acts fall to be filed under Rule 18

@ref O 33 r 30(4) permission question (src:4941)
