-- src:5048 | 45. Nothing in Rules 35, 36, 37, 38, 39 and 40 is to be taken as limiting the right of any shipowner or other person to rely by way of defence on any provision of the Merchant Shipping Act which limits the amount of liability in connection with a ship or other property.
@ref O 33 r 45 (src:5048)
GIVEN `the person is a shipowner or other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person relies by way of defence on a provision of the Merchant Shipping Act which limits the amount of liability in connection with a ship or other property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 45 Rules 35 to 40 limit the right to rely by way of defence on the Merchant Shipping Act` MEANS
    IF `the person is a shipowner or other person` AND `the person relies by way of defence on a provision of the Merchant Shipping Act which limits the amount of liability in connection with a ship or other property`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in Rules 35, 36, 37, 38, 39 and 40 is to be taken as limiting the right of any shipowner or other person to rely by way of defence on any provision of the Merchant Shipping Act which limits the amount of liability in connection with a ship or other property"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text speaks only of these facts

-- src:5050 | 46. —(1) Where, in any action relating to a marine insurance policy, an application for production of documents is made by the insurer under Order 11, Rule 2, then, without affecting its powers under that Rule, the Court may, if satisfied that the circumstances of the case are such that it is necessary or expedient to do so, make an order, either in Form 33 or in such other form as the Court thinks fit, for the production of such documents as are therein specified or described. (2) An order under this Rule may be made on such terms, if any, as to staying proceedings in the action or otherwise, as the Court thinks fit.
@ref O 33 r 46(1) (src:5050)
GIVEN `the action relates to a marine insurance policy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application for production of documents is made by the insurer under Order 11, Rule 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the circumstances of the case are such that it is necessary or expedient to make an order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court makes an order, either in Form 33 or in such other form as the Court thinks fit, for the production of such documents as are therein specified or described` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 46(1) the Court may order the production of documents in a marine insurance action` MEANS
    IF `the action relates to a marine insurance policy` AND `an application for production of documents is made by the insurer under Order 11, Rule 2` AND `the Court is satisfied that the circumstances of the case are such that it is necessary or expedient to make an order`
    THEN IF `the Court makes an order, either in Form 33 or in such other form as the Court thinks fit, for the production of such documents as are therein specified or described`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where, in any action relating to a marine insurance policy, an application for production of documents is made by the insurer under Order 11, Rule 2, then, without affecting its powers under that Rule, the Court may, if satisfied that the circumstances of the case are such that it is necessary or expedient to do so, make an order, either in Form 33 or in such other form as the Court thinks fit, for the production of such documents as are therein specified or described"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, in any action relating to a marine insurance policy, an application for production of documents is made by the insurer under Order 11, Rule 2, then, without affecting its powers under that Rule, the Court may, if satisfied that the circumstances of the case are such that it is necessary or expedient to do so, make an order, either in Form 33 or in such other form as the Court thinks fit, for the production of such documents as are therein specified or described"
